  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of scale, siting and design, would appear overly dominant and unsympathetic when compared with the original dwelling, would result in the loss of openness to a characteristic gap at a prominent corner plot, disrupt the surrounding pattern of development and imbalance the terrace row. The proposal would cause moderate harm to the character and appearance of the host dwelling and surrounding area, including to the historic distinctiveness of the Becontree Estate. The proposal is thus contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that development recognises local character and promotes good design whilst protecting and enhancing historic environments:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies HC1 and D4 of the London Plan (March, 2021)Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4 and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
